Example 1:

Input: nums = [2,0,2,1,1,0]

Output: [0,0,1,1,2,2]

Explanation:

The array has two 0s, two 1s, and two 2s. Sorting them in-place places all 0s first, then all 1s, then all 2s.

Example 2:

Input: nums = [2,0,1]

Output: [0,1,2]

Explanation:

The array has one each of 0, 1, and 2, arranged in-place in the order 0, 1, 2.

 

Constraints:

n == nums.length
1 <= n <= 300
nums[i] is either 0, 1, or 2.

solution:
class Solution {
    public void sortColors(int[] nums) {
        int low=0;
        int mid=0;
        int high=nums.length-1;
        while(mid<=high){
            if(nums[mid]==0){
                int temp=nums[mid];
                nums[mid]=nums[low];
                nums[low]=temp;
                low++;
                mid++;
            }else if(nums[mid]==1){
                mid++;
            }
            else if(nums[mid]==2){
                int temp=nums[mid];
                nums[mid]=nums[high];
                nums[high]=temp;
                high--;
            }
            
        }
        
    }
}
